      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I believe that prioritizing housing allocation by income level is the most equitable because it directly targets the root of economic disparity. While a lottery might seem fair on the surface, it doesn't account for the systemic inequalities that prevent low-income individuals from having equal opportunities. Similarly, while proximity to transit is important, it doesn't address the immediate need for affordable housing among the most vulnerable populations. By focusing on income level, we can ensure that those who need it the most receive the support they deserve, ultimately creating a more just and balanced society.",
